.SS arkuse commands
Every subcommand, machine format, watch frame, config key, update check and
cap notification mirrors
.BR cmduse 's,
with AFP standing where the other binaries put money.
.TP
.B (no command), \fB\-1\fR
Live watch, or one frame with \fB\-1\fR.  The dashboard shows the plan's own
5\-hour / daily / weekly / monthly meter rows, each with the server's share of
the limit and this store's AFP beside it labelled \fIlocal\fR, then a model
block with each model's coefficient, AFP, requests and share of period AFP.
No per\-model allowance is invented: ARK limits the plan.
.TP
.B daily, hourly, session, model
The same reports as
.BR cmduse .
\fB\-\-csv\fR columns are
\fIday|hour|session|model,requests,tokens_in,tokens_out,cache_read,afp\fR
(no cache\-write column, and AFP replaces cost).  \fBmodel\fR with no id prints
the period's per\-model table.
.TP
.B models
The ARK catalogue with the coefficient in force today (a promo halves it until
its date), the derived ¥/1M tokens, the minimum tier and whether the selected
plan grants the model.  \fB\-\-gated\fR keeps only what the plan grants;
\fB\-\-json\fR is one object per line.  Needs no store.
.TP
.B plans
The personal tiers (price, monthly AFP quota, and the 5\-hour / daily / weekly
quotas), the active promos, the flat AFP rate, and the enterprise seat price
list.  Enterprise AFP is metered per seat and the personal usage API does not
expose it, so only prices appear.  Needs no store.
.TP
.B statusline
One compact line: period AFP, 5\-hour AFP, weekly AFP and the top model.
\fB\-\-json\fR mirrors cmduse's keys (\fImonthSpent\fR,
\fIfiveHourSpent\fR, \fIweeklySpent\fR, the caps \fBnull\fR, \fImodel\fR)
with an extra \fIafp\fR block carrying the monthly yuan figure and the
control plane's \fIaccount\fR object.
.TP
.B mcp
Run an MCP stdio server exposing the same seven tools \(em \fIusage\fR,
\fIplans\fR, \fImodels\fR, \fIdaily\fR, \fIhourly\fR, \fIsession\fR,
\fImodel\fR \) whose output matches the subcommands.
.SS arkuse options
The shared options are those under
.BR "ocuse options" ,
with these differences.
.TP
.B \-\-plan \fItier\fR
The ARK tier: \fIsmall\fR, \fImedium\fR, \fIlarge\fR or \fImax\fR.  Default:
the profile's own \fIplan_tier\fR, else \fImedium\fR.  An unknown tier exits 2
and lists the known ones.
.TP
.B \-\-profile \fIname\fR
The \fBarkcli\fR control\-plane profile to query.  Default
\fB$ARKUSE_PROFILE\fR, else the first profile whose type is
\fIagent\-plan\fR.  An unknown name degrades to the local estimate with the
control plane's own reason on the dashboard.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-api
Skip \fBarkcli\fR entirely and report the local estimate only.  The tier then
comes from \fB\-\-plan\fR or the catalogue default, and no profile is
resolved.
.SS arkuse data and windows
Two sources.  \fBarkcli usage plan\fR returns the plan's own meters with their
reset instants \(em the only figures that see every machine and harness on the
subscription \(em and the local stores (\fIopencode.db\fR plus the \fBpi\fR and
\fBdsh\fR session logs, provider \fIagent\-plan\fR only) supply the per\-model
attribution and the local estimate.  The server's windows are not reproducible locally: the 5\-hour
window is a block with its own reset, the week is anchored to Monday 00:00, and
the month is the subscription anniversary, so rows are cut at
\fIreset \(mi window\fR and period dates print in the server's own offset.
A text\-only workload has no daily window; only media and Harness items do.
When no meter answers the rows fall back to a rolling cut and the block is
labelled \fIestimated locally\fR with the reason beside it \(em still as
\fIused / quota\fR against the plan's published split (5\-hour 10%, daily 50%,
weekly 35%, monthly 100% of its AFP), with a percentage and a countdown, so a
window never degrades to AFP alone.  A meter served without figures (a
just\-reset block carries only \fItotal\fR and \fIpercent\fR) is derived rather
than rejected, and its countdown comes from the oldest row still inside the
cut.
.PP
The plan's semantics are surfaced rather than assumed: no downgrade; on an
upgrade the monthly quota is pro\-rated while the 5\-hour and weekly windows
reset to the new tier immediately; plain API calls against the plan base URL
are forbidden (ban risk); the quota is shared across every harness; and
postpaid overflow is opt\-in.  Because ARK limits the plan rather than a model,
\fInotify_on_cap\fR fires per window meter.  The model block states each
model's month AFP and tokens without a share of its own: a \fITOP 3 MODELS\fR
block above the table carries the period's split (AFP and its share of period
AFP, then tokens and their share of all tokens), and the \fIperiod:\fR line
ends with the control plane's own monthly share, \fIN% of limit\fR, verbatim
(\fI53\fR, never \fI53.0\fR), whenever an account answered.
.SS arkuse files
.TP
.I ~/.config/arkuse/config.json
The same keys as cmduse's config, set with \fBarkuse config set\fR.
.TP
.I $OPENCODE_DB, \-\-db
The store path; opened read\-only.
